  "title": "A growing plane reads taxicab distance in conformal time",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "For every doubling schedule from the open n x n tube of rule-60 rings with law (12, 12) contacts (n >= 3, g >= 2): (Lemma 1) one-stage earliest arrivals are the steps to the next contact, g times the contact lattice's hop distance, and the steps from the last contact; (Theorem 2) whenever T1(v) is defined, 4g d(v) - 6g <= phi(T1(v)) <= 4g d(v) + 9g + 2 in conformal time (A56), with T1(v) defined once the schedule's conformal length reaches the upper bound; (Corollary 3) the conformal round trip satisfies the triangle inequality up to 42g + 4.",
